Q: How to call a model method including a parameter from a CodeIgniter controller A: <p>I have noticed that you <strong>used</strong> to post the value of <code>id</code> in your code:</p>

<p><code>echo '&lt;a href="' . base_url() . 'administrator/delete?id=' . $row-&gt;cust_id . '"&gt;Delete&lt;/a&gt;';</code></p>

<p>while on your controller you used the <code>get()</code> using the name of <code>cust_id</code>:</p>

<p><code>$this-&gt;admin_model-&gt;delete($this-&gt;input-&gt;get('cust_id'));</code></p>

<p>you cannot get any value because <code>cust_id</code> is not the name of the posted value. so change your <code>cust_id</code> to <code>id</code> like the example below:</p>

<pre><code>public function delete() {
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('admin_model');
    $this-&gt;admin_model-&gt;delete($this-&gt;input-&gt;get('id'));
    $this-&gt;customer();
}
</code></pre>
